- `workspace-project handoff-check axi-workbench`: `score 10 / errors 0 /
  warnings 0`.
- `workspace:audit`: 0 errors.

## Why three commits, not one

The workbench merge (commit 6bf7d674) is a workbench-only
event. The governance-registry cleanup is a governance-only
event that follows it. Mixing the two would cross-cut
governance review and workbench review — the governance
repo has its own ADRs, its own workweek cadence, and its
own admission-decision protocol. Keeping the cleanup as a
separate chore (this patch) preserves that boundary.

## Out of scope for this patch

- Removing the source repos from `/Volumes/code/workspace/products/`
  and `/Volumes/code/workspace/projects/`. Those directories are
  already moved to `/Volumes/code/workspace/references/archives/
  2026-09-20/repo/` (with local archive tags on the source repos);
  the governance patch does not need to touch the filesystem.
- Renaming or removing the AGENTS.md / PRD.md / ARCHIVE.md in the
  source repos. Those are part of the source repos' local history
  (already committed under tag `archive/<name>/2026-09-20`).
- Updating `docs/content/{en,zh}/projects/<merged-project>/` in
  `axi-workbench/apps/axi-docs/app/docs/`. The doc content
  reorganisation is a separate `axi-docs` chore that can land
  on a separate branch.
